    "created_at": "2020-06-04T05:08:25Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-06-04T05:08:25Z",
    "body": "Respecting EXIF for images is fine and is indeed opaque if it always happens everywhere. `image-orientation` allows it to be disabled via `none`, thus presenting an information leak when that happens for opaque response images. These new getters would also leak it, thus presenting an information leak. I don't think we should allow either.",
